# Cloudflare Pages routing.
#
# Deliberately empty of rewrite rules.
#
# Every route is prerendered to its own index.html, including /admin, so Pages
# resolves each one as a real file and returns its own 404.html for anything
# else. A catch-all like `/* /index.html 200` would answer unknown URLs with 200
# and the homepage, i.e. a soft 404: Google treats those as thin duplicates of
# `/` and they compete with real pages in the index.
#
# Leaving this file (with just comments) documents that the absence of a
# fallback is intentional rather than an oversight.
